<section>
<title>Detailed Description</title>

<para>An AnimMesh is an attachment to an <link linkend="_structai_mesh">aiMesh</link> stores per-vertex animations for a particular frame. </para>



<para>You may think of an <link linkend="_structai_anim_mesh">aiAnimMesh</link> as a <computeroutput>patch</computeroutput> for the host mesh, which replaces only certain vertex data streams at a particular time. Each mesh stores n attached attached meshes (<link linkend="_structai_mesh_1a5078f7db7e99ed05db89dfa412f0e990">aiMesh::mAnimMeshes</link>). The actual relationship between the time line and anim meshes is established by <link linkend="_structai_mesh_anim">aiMeshAnim</link>, which references singular mesh attachments by their ID and binds them to a time offset. </para>
</section>
